{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>From the ram of ordination that belongs to Aaron.</b> He did not mention his sons, and the ram is an ordination offering for all of them. The sense of it is that Scripture commands <b>And you shall take the breast of the wave-offering from the ram of ordination</b> because it belongs to Aaron, and the breast is not fitting for him, for it shall not belong to the owners. And once he has given the reason that it is not fitting that it belong to Aaron, there is no need to say that it shall not belong to his sons, for after him they shall inherit it. And below it says (Exodus 29:27) \"that which belongs to Aaron and that which belongs to his sons,\" meaning: just as the breast and thigh are taken from the offering of all of them, so shall they — the father and the sons — take from the offerings of those who bring sacrifices through their hands:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:18:06.996765012Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}